>  f - 2 cursed scrolls of create monster
>  k - an uncursed wand of create monster

Given that you have these, and an altar high in the dungeon, and are
pretty well kitted-out, I'd suggest first sacfesting to raise your
luck and make sure your god is happy with you. You mention that you
have luck problems; you should be able to generate lots of easy
monsters with those items (creating them on a high dungeon level will
mean they're relatively easy); lock the doors to the room if possible
(you don't have an IDed wand of locking, so you won't be able to
create doors in empty doorways), and create monsters to sacrifice on
the altar (just don't sacrifice monsters of your own race or coaligned
unicorns; you won't create any former pets like this, but don't
sacrifice those either if you find them). You'll likely get your luck
up to maximum like that.

After that, I'd suggest doing the Quest; be careful around drawbridges
(blow them up yourself if you can, say with a wand of striking, to
prevent instadeath by them being broken while you're standing on
them). Your lack of reflection may potentially be a problem, as on the
Valkyrie Quest there are intelligent monsters which can use wands, and
a random /oDeath could be a disaster; but on the other hand you may
get useful loot there, and you have to go there anywhere. Another
possibility is to go down to Medusa (which shouldn't be difficult
given your stats) and hope to get a shield of reflection in the statue
of Perseus, but you'll need to find a way to cross water. (Those un-
IDed jungle boots might be boots of levitation, if you have no further
information about them. You could also try identifying those cursed
rings, just in case; after sacfesting you should have plenty of luck,
and the ability to gain holy water via water prayer, so that you can
ID at least 2 items, and possibly more, with each scroll of ID.) I
personally find doing the Castle without MR inadvisable due to the
chance of liches, so I wouldn't advise digging down below Medusa due
to the chance you have problems getting back up again.

